# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TheGreenFeed environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and must never be committed. These are placeholders only — never
# put real credentials in this tracked file.
#
# Supabase: Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# These names match the Vercel project environment exactly. None is prefixed
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_, so all are server-only and never exposed to the browser.
#   - Project URL            → SUPABASE_URL
#   - Publishable key        → SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#     (a legacy "anon" key can be used here if your project has not migrated
#      to publishable keys yet)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only secret. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Only required if survey submissions are inserted through the server-side
# route using the privileged client. Keep it out of client bundles.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development-only survey preview (do NOT set in production).
# While the survey is unpublished, setting SURVEY_DEV_PREVIEW=1 in a
# development environment (e.g. `.env.development.local`) lets you walk
# through the full experience locally. Production builds always ignore it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SURVEY_DEV_PREVIEW=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin panel (server-only). None of these is prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# The admin area is disabled unless ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET is set (32+ random
# chars) AND at least one password variable is set.
#   - ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH : preferred. Generate it with
#       node scripts/hash-admin-password.mjs "your password"
#     and paste the printed `scrypt:<saltHex>:<hashHex>` value here.
#   - ADMIN_PASSWORD      : fallback plaintext, compared in constant time.
#     Use only if you cannot store the hash.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: canonical site origin used for absolute metadata URLs
# (Open Graph/Twitter images). Defaults to the production Vercel URL when unset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thegreenfeed-p385.vercel.app
